  "result": "Reservations with expiry are in, and `npm test` passes (174 tests, 0 failed). Nine of those are new tests in `test/reservations.test.js`; the other 165 are the existing ones.\n\n- **Store (`src/store.js`):**\n  - `reserve`, `confirm`, `release` and `getAvailable` follow your spec, and `removeItem` now checks against available stock.\n  - `getStock` still returns physical stock.\n  - Expiry uses only the `clock` option, so a reservation stops counting at exactly creation time plus `ttlMs`.\n  - Reservation ids look like `res-1`, `res-2`, and so on.\n- **API (`src/api.js`):**\n  - `GET /stock/:sku` now includes `available`.\n  - `POST /reservations`, `POST /reservations/:id/confirm` and `DELETE /reservations/:id` return the statuses you listed.\n\nI made two choices where the spec was silent:\n- An expired reservation stays stored, so confirming it repeatedly keeps returning `RESERVATION_EXPIRED` rather than \"not found\". Nothing cleans expired ones up.\n- `ttlMs` isn't validated. On `POST /reservations`, any error other than `INSUFFICIENT_STOCK` returns 400 with the error message.\n\nOne stray line appeared after the test output: `/usr/bin/bash: line 177: /c: Is a directory`. It looks like a shell-profile quirk rather than anything from the tests.",
